{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0123","billNumberShort":"S.B. 123","billNumberLong":"SB0123S02","fileNumber":"2026FL0177","shortTitle":"Privacy and Cybersecurity Amendments","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"HARPEWA","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Harper, Wayne A.","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"WILCORD","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Wilcox, Ryan D.","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies provisions related to the Utah Cyber Center.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>adds the Department of Environmental Quality an as entity that the Utah Cyber Center will collaborate with when performing legislative duties; <hr><ltbullet>modifies the deadline for developing a statewide strategic cybersecurity plan;<hr><ltbullet>expands the Utah Cyber Center's duties to include local education agencies;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the composition of the Cybersecurity Commission to include a representative from the Utah Education and Telehealth Network; <hr><ltbullet>creates the Utah Cyber Center Restricted Account (account) and makes appropriations from the account nonlapsing; <hr><ltbullet>repeals a section related to government cybersecurity; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Scott Elder","fiscalAnalyst":"Steven M. Allred","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/17/2026","trackingID":"WUDIYUBEKD","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-12 13:44:46.890","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-12 13:44:46.907","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","